# The BIMI mark is frozen artwork. Its bytes must match what the CA validated,
# so Git must never rewrite line endings in this repository.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows (core.autocrlf=true by default) rewrites the
# 6 LF bytes in logo.svg to CRLF on checkout. That makes the file 1682 bytes
# instead of 1676 and changes its SHA-256 completely, which invalidates the
# certified artwork and silently kills the inbox logo.

* -text
logo.svg binary
